{% include "components/site-header.njk" %}

<div class="max-w-4xl mx-auto px-4 py-12">
  <h1 class="text-4xl font-bold mb-6">Book Collection JSON Schema</h1>

  <p class="text-lg mb-6">This page documents the JSON schema for the <a href="/data/books.json" class="text-blue-600 hover:underline">/data/books.json</a> endpoint.</p>

  <section class="mb-8">
    <h2 class="text-2xl font-semibold mb-4">Overview</h2>
    <p class="mb-4">The books collection is an array of book objects, each containing comprehensive bibliographic and physical metadata. Every object carries the same 39 keys, the 37 catalogue columns plus <code class="bg-gray-100 px-1 rounded-sm">collection</code> and <code class="bg-gray-100 px-1 rounded-sm">cover_url</code>; all values are strings, and an unrecorded field is an empty string rather than <code class="bg-gray-100 px-1 rounded-sm">null</code>.</p>

    <h3 class="text-xl font-semibold mb-2">Key Fields</h3>
    <ul class="list-disc pl-6 space-y-2">
      <li><code class="bg-gray-100 px-2 py-1 rounded-sm">title</code> - Book title</li>
      <li><code class="bg-gray-100 px-2 py-1 rounded-sm">author_full_name</code> - Primary author name</li>
      <li><code class="bg-gray-100 px-2 py-1 rounded-sm">isbn_asin</code> - ISBN or ASIN identifier</li>
      <li><code class="bg-gray-100 px-2 py-1 rounded-sm">publisher</code> - Publishing house</li>
      <li><code class="bg-gray-100 px-2 py-1 rounded-sm">publication_year</code> - Year of publication</li>
      <li><code class="bg-gray-100 px-2 py-1 rounded-sm">description</code> - Book description</li>
      <li><code class="bg-gray-100 px-2 py-1 rounded-sm">image_url</code> - Cover image path as recorded in the catalogue, which may be blank even where a cover exists</li>
      <li><code class="bg-gray-100 px-2 py-1 rounded-sm">cover_url</code> - Site-root-relative path to the cover, checked against the published files: it always resolves, and is empty only when the library holds no cover for the book. Prefer this to <code class="bg-gray-100 px-1 rounded-sm">image_url</code> when you want the picture</li>
      <li><code class="bg-gray-100 px-2 py-1 rounded-sm">collection_grouping</code> - Thematic collection membership</li>
      <li><code class="bg-gray-100 px-2 py-1 rounded-sm">tags</code> - Comma-separated subject tags</li>
      <li><code class="bg-gray-100 px-2 py-1 rounded-sm">collection</code> - The wing the record belongs to (<code class="bg-gray-100 px-1 rounded-sm">art</code>, <code class="bg-gray-100 px-1 rounded-sm">cryptology</code>, <code class="bg-gray-100 px-1 rounded-sm">hacking</code>)</li>
    </ul>
  </section>

